<title>GERMANY: Schmalbach 1996 net profit 51 mln dmk.</title>
<headline>Schmalbach 1996 net profit 51 mln dmk.</headline>
<dateline>RATINGEN, Germany 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   51	vs 0</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		   193     vs 118</p>
<p>    Group sales				  4,089   vs 4,124</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (DVFA)		19.26   vs 7.09</p>
<p>    Group gross cash flow		    275     vs 263</p>
<p>    Cash flow per share			73.33   vs 70.13</p>
<p>    Total investments			  317     vs 297</p>
<p>    Return on equity (in percent)	  22.7    vs 19.0</p>
<p>    Workforce				    12,351  vs 12,612</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German packaging producer is Schmalbach-Lubeca AG, a unit of the utility group Viag AG.</p>
<p>Schmalbach said it expected sales of around four billion marks in 1997 and that net profit would be higher than 1996 due to extraordinary income from the sale of its metals packaging business.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
